[29.79421, "o", "Help on class EventClock in module bytewax.operators.windowing:\r\n\r\nclass E\bEv\bve\ben\bnt\btC\bCl\blo\boc\bck\bk(Clock)\r\n"]
[29.794389, "o", " |  EventClock(ts_getter: Callable[[~V], datetime.datetime], wait_for_system_duration: datetime.timedelta, now_getter: Callable[[], datetime.datetime] = <functi\r\non _get_system_utc at 0x7d611fbba200>, to_system_utc: Callable[[datetime.datetime], Optional[datetime.datetime]] = <function _identity at 0x7d612054e200>) -> No\r\nne\r\n"]
[29.794444, "o", " |\r\n |  Use a timestamp embedded within each item.\r\n |\r\n"]
[29.794605, "o", " |  The watermark is the largest timestamp seen thus far, minus the\r\n |  waiting duration, plus the system time duration that has elapsed\r\n |  since that item was seen. This effectively means that items will\r\n"]
[29.794656, "o", " |  be correctly processed as long as they do not have timestamps\r\n"]
[29.794704, "o", " |  out-of-order or arrive later than the waiting duration.\r\n |\r\n |  :::{note}\r\n |\r\n"]
[29.794841, "o", " |  By default, all timestamps returned by `ts_getter` also need to be\r\n |  [aware datetimes](inv:python:std:label#datetime-naive-aware) in\r\n |  UTC.\r\n |\r\n |  This is because `now_getter` defaults to returning the current\r\n"]
[29.794887, "o", " |  system time as [aware\r\n |  datetimes](inv:python:std:label#datetime-naive-aware) in UTC, and\r\n"]
[29.794988, "o", " |  comparisons are made to that.\r\n |\r\n |  It's easiest to convert your timestamps to UTC in `ts_getter`, but\r\n"]
[29.795035, "o", " |  you can also specify a custom `now_getter` and `to_system_utc` to\r\n |  support other sense of time.\r\n |\r\n |  :::\r\n"]
[29.795158, "o", " |\r\n |  :arg ts_getter: Called once on each item to get its timestamp.\r\n |\r\n |  :arg wait_for_system_duration: How much system time to wait after\r\n"]
[29.795241, "o", " |      seeing a timestamp to have the watermark catch up to that time.\r\n |\r\n"]
[29.79529, "o", " |  :arg now_getter: Return the current \"system\" timestamp used to\r\n |      advance the watermark. Defaults to the current system time in\r\n"]
[29.795394, "o", "\u001b[7m--More--\u001b[27m"]
