[36.316698, "o", "Help on class TumblingWindower in module bytewax.operators.windowing:\r\n\r\nclass T\bTu\bum\bmb\bbl\bli\bin\bng\bgW\bWi\bin\bnd\bdo\bow\bwe\ber\br(Windower)\r\n"]
[36.31677, "o", " |  TumblingWindower(length: datetime.timedelta, align_to: datetime.datetime) -> None\r\n |\r\n |  Tumbling windows of fixed duration.\r\n |\r\n |  Each item will fall in exactly one window.\r\n |\r\n"]
[36.316821, "o", " |  Window open times are inclusive, but close times are exclusive.\r\n |\r\n |  :::{warning}\r\n |\r\n"]
[36.316875, "o", " |  Changing any of the windowing parameters across executions will\r\n"]
[36.316929, "o", " |  result in incorrect output for any windows that were open at the\r\n |  time of the resume snapshot.\r\n |\r\n |  :::\r\n |\r\n"]
[36.316978, "o", " |  :arg length: Length of windows.\r\n |\r\n"]
[36.317027, "o", " |  :arg align_to: Align windows so this instant starts a window. You\r\n |      can use this to align all windows to an hour boundary, e.g.\r\n |\r\n"]
[36.317316, "o", " |  Method resolution order:\r\n |      TumblingWindower\r\n |      Windower\r\n |      abc.ABC\r\n |      typing.Generic\r\n |      builtins.object\r\n |\r\n |  Methods defined here:\r\n |\r\n |  _\b__\b_e\beq\bq_\b__\b_(self, other)\r\n |      Return self==value.\r\n |\r\n |  _\b__\b_i\bin\bni\bit\bt_\b__\b_(self, length: datetime.timedelta, align_to: datetime.datetime) -> None\r\n |      Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\r\n |\r\n"]
